Cell[TextData[StyleBox["The worksheet functions below create the following \
Matematica matrix definitions from the table above:\nST_matrix - the \
Stoichiometric matrix, \nOBJ - the objective function, the last row in the \
excel table and the first argument of the LinearProgramming function. These \
constraints are set to maximize growth, or as far as the LinearProgramming \
function is concerned, we are minimizing negative growth, which is why the \
OBJ_F coefficent for Rar is -1.\nLP_matrix - the second argument of the \
LinearProgramming function. Its all of the columns in the Stoichiometric \
matrix, intersected with the Stoichiometric matrix rows and the rows \
containing the metabolite influx constraints, C_G and C_O.\nConstraints - the \
third argument of the LinearProgramming function. Two columns, a threshold \
level and an equality type code. The row count must match the number of rows \
in LP_matrix.",
  FontFamily->"Comic Sans MS",
  FontSize->9]], "Input",
  FormatType->TextForm],

